# Color scheme

`docs/color-scheme.md` is the palette. `app/lib/app/app_theme.dart` is the only place colors are defined. Screens use `appTheme()`, `AppColors`, `dangerTextStyle()`, and `dangerFilledStyle()`.

- Primary `FilledButton` continues the task.
- Secondary `OutlinedButton` is a real choice that is not the main one.
- Quiet `TextButton` leaves, cancels, or opens a side path.
- Danger text is `dangerTextStyle()`. It opens a dangerous step or removes one item. Center it when it is the only control in that block.
- Danger fill is `dangerFilledStyle()`. It commits the harm. White label on `#B91C1C`.
- Error text uses `colorScheme.error` (`#F87171`).

Red is only for danger and errors. Do not add a hex color on a widget. Warning and success wait until a screen needs them.
